course: dictionary
lesson: 8598
title: Scorpion: an animal or a star sign
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. «Spiders are arachnids, together with scorpions, ticks and mites.» Spiders, ticks and mites are all animals, so a scorpion must be an animal too.
explain: Look for clues around the word. «The elf owl ... eats moths, crickets and even scorpions.» Owls eat small animals, so a scorpion must be a creature a small owl can catch. Ask: what would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Scorpio is a different meaning. It is a star sign and a constellation, the group of stars in the night sky. If a sentence talks about birthdays or the stars, check whether it means Scorpio rather than the animal. When context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: A scorpion is a small animal with eight legs, two pincers like a crab and a curved tail with a poisonous sting at the end.
fact: Scorpions are arachnids, like spiders, not insects.
fact: Scorpions live in hot, dry places such as deserts in the USA and Australia.
fact: «Scorpions glow blue-green under ultraviolet light», and scientists are still not sure why.
fact: Only a few dozen of more than 2,000 kinds have venom dangerous to people, but none should be picked up.
exercise: «Spiders are arachnids, together with scorpions, ticks and mites.» What kind of thing is a scorpion here? | *An animal | A kind of plant | A type of rock | A star in the sky
exercise: Scorpions have how many legs? | Two | Six | *Eight | Ten
exercise: Which word names the star sign rather than the animal? | Scorpion | Meerkat | Spider | *Scorpio
test: «Scorpions glow blue-green under ultraviolet light.» Under which kind of light do scorpions glow? | Red light | Moonlight | *Ultraviolet light | Candlelight
test: In a meerkat group, one meerkat stands on a rock as a guard while the rest dig for beetles. What job does the meerkat on the rock do? | To dig for beetles | To eat a scorpion | To sleep in the sun | *To guard the group
exam: Which statement is true? | Scorpions are insects with six legs | *Scorpions are arachnids, not insects | Scorpions live in the snow of the Arctic | All scorpions are dangerous to people
